    {
      "id": "p0028-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Sometimes, it's not the words themselves that are difficult to translate, but how they're presented. Literal translations tend to fall apart when this type of \"creative packaging\" is involved. Here are a few simple examples.",
        "raw": "Sometimes, it's not the words themselves that are difficult to translate, but\nhow they're presented. Literal translations tend to fall apart when this type of\n\"creative packaging\" is involved. Here are a few simple examples.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28621192,
          0.08880714,
          0.89046741,
          0.1371
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28419022,
          0.08809286,
          0.90352759,
          0.13817143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "有时难译的不是词语本身，而是它们的呈现方式。碰上这种“创意包装”，直译往往会失效。下面是几个简单例子。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
