    {
      "id": "p0028-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Writers sometimes include meticulously worded hints meant to guide the reader or lead the reader astray. Such hints might be used as mystery clues, as foreshadowing devices, or to say something indirectly. Naturally, a carefully crafted hint can easily break during translation.",
        "raw": "Writers sometimes include meticulously worded hints meant to guide the\nreader or lead the reader astray. Such hints might be used as mystery clues, as\nforeshadowing devices, or to say something indirectly. Naturally, a carefully\ncrafted hint can easily break during translation.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29175138,
          0.17954286,
          0.88647456,
          0.24781429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28419022,
          0.17882857,
          0.90352759,
          0.24888571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          6,
          7,
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "作者有时会用精心斟酌的措辞引导读者，或把读者引向歧途。这些提示可以是谜题线索、伏笔，也可以用来委婉表达。这样的精巧安排，自然很容易在翻译中失灵。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
