    {
      "id": "p0028-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Rhyme, rhythm, and syllable counts are important in poetry, but tend to get lost in a literal translation. For example, a literal translation of a Japanese haiku into English will probably have too many syllables to still be a traditional haiku.",
        "raw": "Rhyme, rhythm, and syllable counts are important in poetry, but tend to get lost\nin a literal translation. For example, a literal translation of a Japanese haiku\ninto English will probably have too many syllables to still be a traditional haiku.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29268136,
          0.28990714,
          0.90150589,
          0.33957143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28419022,
          0.28919286,
          0.90352759,
          0.34064286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          11,
          12,
          13
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "押韵、节奏和音节数对诗歌很重要，却往往在直译中丢失。例如，把日语俳句直译成英语，音节通常会多到不再符合传统俳句的形式。",
        "status": "draft",
