    {
      "id": "p0028-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Songs present a similar creative packaging problem. A literal translation of \"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer\" into Japanese, for example, will result in lyrics that no longer fit the music. The natural solution, then, is to tweak the translation until they do fit the music:",
        "raw": "Songs present a similar creative packaging problem. A literal translation of\n\"Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer\" into Japanese, for example, will result in\nlyrics that no longer fit the music. The natural solution, then, is to tweak the\ntranslation until they do fit the music:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28667691,
          0.38132857,
          0.8754563,
          0.44960714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
